00:44:14.184 --> 00:44:17.254
I do play Tom, like, he don't really, like,
focus on me like that.

00:44:17.254 --> 00:44:20.924
He's so focused on his game and trying
to be the best quarterback that he can be.

00:44:21.258 --> 00:44:23.227
And I kind of just can, I can just play.

00:44:23.227 --> 00:44:24.728
And that's
with all the greats. You know? That's

00:44:24.728 --> 00:44:26.430
with all the greats.
I don't know, Aaron Rodgers

00:44:26.430 --> 00:44:30.934
they was chipping me a little bit, too. Like,
Aaron Rodgers, when we played them this year,
they was whipping me, man.
- You should be getting chipped.

00:44:31.835 --> 00:44:34.104
You should be getting chipped, by the way, a lot.

00:44:35.272 --> 00:44:38.275
Like, that's smart football. Like, who's not gonna,
you've gotta get some chips, man.

00:44:38.342 --> 00:44:40.110
- I just wanna line up anc play football, man.

00:44:40.110 --> 00:44:43.514
I just wanna line up and play football, man. But, um-
- You just wanna hurt the quarterback and get sack-fumbles
 and get sacks.

00:44:43.514 --> 00:44:47.785
- I don't, I don't. I go for the ball every time.
- You can't do that all day.

00:44:49.086 --> 00:44:51.288
I go for the ball every time. I'm not trying to...,

00:44:51.288 --> 00:44:54.091
They're the premier players in our league.
- You're gonna hurt their arm or something.

00:44:54.091 --> 00:44:56.794
Like, you gotta, like, you're one of the best

00:44:56.827 --> 00:45:00.330
edge-rushers in history, bro.
You've gotta get chipped.

00:45:00.330 --> 00:45:01.799
- Bruh, you say you like going against Cover 1,

00:45:01.799 --> 00:45:03.434
I like going against the greats.

00:45:03.434 --> 00:45:05.502
- Hopefully we play y'all in the Super Bowl.

00:45:05.569 --> 00:45:09.139
- I hope-
- Bro, we game-plan against you. You know that, right?

00:45:09.139 --> 00:45:15.813
We try to chip you. With Tom at quarterback,
no matter who it is. [Laughing]

00:45:15.813 --> 00:45:19.183
- I got one more question, man, and then I'm gonna let you go, man.
I appreciate you, bro.

00:45:19.216 --> 00:45:22.186
What is the worst weather
that you've ever played in?

00:45:22.419 --> 00:45:23.954
This is from Asia Brown.
- Yeah,

00:45:23.954 --> 00:45:28.025
we played Baltimore in 2018.

00:45:28.592 --> 00:45:32.496
I think it was Lamar Jackson's
rookie year. Man, it was like 30 degrees,

00:45:32.963 --> 00:45:36.500
but it was pouring down raining, and it was-
- So it wasn't snowing yet.

00:45:36.834 --> 00:45:40.037
- The ball felt like a brick,
nah, it wasn't snow, it was just rain.

00:45:40.738 --> 00:45:44.341
I think both teams combined
had like 15, 20 drops

00:45:44.608 --> 00:45:47.978
in one game.
I'll say, I'll say like 10 to 15.

00:45:48.312 --> 00:45:50.547
But the ball was like a brick.

00:45:50.547 --> 00:45:53.250
It was super slick, tough game.

00:45:53.250 --> 00:45:55.652
And Lamar Jackson went off on us
too that game,

00:45:55.686 --> 00:45:59.723
by the way. He's a rookie, making real good
plays in the rain and cold.

00:46:01.125 --> 00:46:01.692
- Just scrambling,

00:46:01.692 --> 00:46:02.593
my boy.

00:46:03.260 --> 00:46:04.895
Um, you know, kstidge said:

00:46:04.895 --> 00:46:07.598
I knew I loved Mike Evans,

00:46:07.598 --> 00:46:11.969
but he loves Harry Potter, and he's now
my favorite receiver of all time.

00:46:12.236 --> 00:46:14.638
That's kstidge?
- My man.
- That's love.

00:46:15.105 --> 00:46:19.710
This is my guy, Mike Evans, man. Ay, my Aggie
brother, man, my brother in real life.

00:46:19.710 --> 00:46:22.446
Man, I appreciate you taking time
out of your day.

00:46:22.446 --> 00:46:24.515
I know the family's well.
You've got a beautiful family,

00:46:24.815 --> 00:46:27.117
but I just wanted to send blessings
to all of y'all, man.

00:46:27.751 --> 00:46:31.955
It's an honor and a privilege to do this
Voncast with you and to talk to you on

00:46:31.955 --> 00:46:34.391
on your off day,
man. It's all love and respect.

00:46:34.792 --> 00:46:39.062
If you ever need me for anything, man,
if you just want me to come to

00:46:39.129 --> 00:46:40.764
when your daughter grows up

00:46:40.764 --> 00:46:42.833
and you want me to come dance
at the wedding, man.

00:46:43.066 --> 00:46:44.568
I'll come dance at the wedding, man.

00:46:44.568 --> 00:46:46.203
Whatever you want me to do, man.

00:46:46.203 --> 00:46:48.272
I'm forever in debt to you, my boy.

00:46:48.272 --> 00:46:50.140
I love you, man.
And I appreciate you, man.

00:46:50.140 --> 00:46:51.575
And I wish you the very best.

00:46:51.575 --> 00:46:53.410
And we'll see you in the Super Bowl, my boy.

00:46:55.112 --> 00:46:56.446
- I like the sound of that, man.

00:46:56.446 --> 00:46:58.382
I appreciate you, bro.
Thanks for having me.

00:46:58.382 --> 00:47:01.752
And I still remember you
throwing up at 5:45 workouts

00:47:02.219 --> 00:47:04.688
during the NFL lockout my freshman year.

00:47:05.189 --> 00:47:08.525
That was cool, man. You was out there getting it.

00:47:08.525 --> 00:47:10.994
- Bruh, I was trying to come and still like,
'cause it ain't nothing

00:47:10.994 --> 00:47:12.863
like working out in college, bro.
You know, like,

00:47:12.863 --> 00:47:14.865
you don't really work like that.
- Oh, you can't beat them workouts.

00:47:15.432 --> 00:47:15.933
- Oh, man.

00:47:15.933 --> 00:47:19.203
Well, I was trying to come back and,
you know, work out with Tony and Cyrus,

00:47:19.369 --> 00:47:22.606
you know, still be a part of, like,
Texas A&amp;M, but them boys was getting it.

00:47:22.606 --> 00:47:25.075
I ain't ran like that since then. [Laughing]

00:47:26.276 --> 00:47:26.977
Hey, love, man.

00:47:26.977 --> 00:47:29.112
I appreciate you, my boy.
- All right, big bro.
- Yes, sir.

00:47:29.112 --> 00:47:30.080
Much success, bro.

